{title: 335 - What a Wonderful Savior}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #335 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 335}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Christ has [D/A]for sin atonement made, What a wonderful Savior!
[Em/B]We are redeemed! the price is paid! [D/A]What a wonderful [Em/G]Savior!
[D/F#]What a [A/E]wonderful Savior is [D/F#]Jesus, my Jesus!
[D]What a wonderful Savior [G/D]is Jesus, [D]my Lord!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Em/B]What a wonderful [D/A]Savior
[A7]is Jesus, my Jesus!
[A7/G]What a wonderful Savior
[D/F#]is Jesus, my Lord!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]I [D/A]praise Him for the cleansing blood,
[Em/B]What a wonderful [D/A]Saviour!
[D/F#]That reconciled [A]my [D/F#]soul to God;
[D]What a wonderful [G/D]Saviour!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]He [D/A]walks beside me all [G/D]the [D]way,
[Em/B]What a wonderful [D/A]Saviour!
[D/F#]And keeps [A/E]me faithful [D/F#]day by day;
[D]What a wonderful [G/D]Saviour!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[A]He gives [D/A]me overcoming [G/D]power,
[Em/B]What a wonderful [D/A]Saviour!
[D/F#]And [A/E]triumph in each [D/F#]trying hour;
[D]What a wonderful [G/D]Saviour!
{end_of_verse}
